  {
   "id": 544965,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In J.K. Rowling’s <i>Harry Potter</i> series, Albus Dumbledore was the headmaster of Hogwarts for many years. Imagine that an election is to be held to find his successor. Severus Snape, the head of Slytherin House, will be running against the heads of Gryffindor and Ravenclaw, Minerva McGonagall and Filius Flitwick. Use the preference rankings for each candidate in the following table to construct a pairwise comparison matrix.\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Percentage of Vote</th>\n<th>25%</th>\n<th>40%</th>\n<th>35%</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>(S) Snape</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(M) McGonagall</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>(F) Flitwick</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 544966,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Analyze the pairwise comparison matrix you constructed for question 51. Display the pairings in a table and indicate the winner of each matchup.",
